# Git and PR conventions

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` and `.github/workflows/pr_lint.yml`.

## Branch naming

`<github-username>/<scope>/<short-description>` (kebab-case, no trailing slash)

Examples: `jdoe/anthropic/normalize-tool-call-ids`, `jdoe/core/vector-store-type-hints`

## PR title (Conventional Commits)

Format: `type(scope): description`

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`, `release`, `hotfix`
- Scopes: `core`, `langchain`, `langchain-classic`, `model-profiles`, `standard-tests`, `text-splitters`, `docs`, partner names (`anthropic`, `openai`, ...), `infra`, `deps`, `partners`
- Scope is REQUIRED for `langchain` package changes — never omit it.
- Start description with lowercase unless first word is a proper noun or code symbol.
- Wrap code symbols in backticks: `feat(langchain): \`ls_agent_type\` tag on \`create_agent\``

Examples:

```txt
feat(anthropic): add streaming retry helper
fix(core): resolve type hinting issue in vector store
test(openai): update API usage tests
```

## PR description

- No `# Summary` header — the description IS the summary.
- Lead with `Fixes #123` (or `Closes`/`Resolves`) when applicable, then `---`, then body.
- Explain **why**: who benefits, what problem, how this solves it.
- Wrap class/function/method names in backticks; do not cite line numbers.
- Skip dedicated "Test plan" sections unless coverage is non-obvious.
- Add a brief disclaimer noting AI-agent involvement.
- All contributions must be in English.

## Pre-PR commands

From the modified package directory:

```bash
make format && make lint && make test
```

Or run `.cursor/scripts/pre_pr.sh <package-path> "<pr-title>"`.
